Root agent self-review found PCB counterexamples had all used default A/SYS_B_P target, which can hide shorts at A_TX_P/A_RX_P when receiver is OFF. Corrected each case to its actual source cabin and hazard node; added an independent test of all three surviving shorts. No physical pass was claimed. Separately full base64 archive assembly first exceeded Linux single-argument limit; no bytes were written. Seven SHA-pinned 64KiB blocks were then assembled individually and full SHA verified.
